t satisfies the requirements and budget. If files conflict, use source dates and the recency rule in `requirements.md`.\n\nCreate the deliverables listed in `output_contract.md` inside an `answer/` folder in this task folder. The goal is to leave behind useful work artifacts that another operations teammate could review.\n\nYour work must make the source-resolution step, vendor screening step, and final purchasing recommendation visible as separate checkpoints.\n\n--- requirements.md ---\n# Requirements\n\nRequest date: 2026-04-30\n\nOrder need: 12 rugged tablets for the field inspection team.\n\nBudget maximum: $2,200 total, including all selected units and required included accessories.\n\nNeed-by date: delivery no later than 2026-05-17.\n\nHard requirements:\n\n- Quantity must be 12 units.\n- Screen size must be at least 10.0 inches.\n- Battery rating must be at least 10 hours.\n- Rugged case must be included in the quoted price.\n- Warranty must be at least 12 months.\n\nSelection rule:\n\n- Reject vendors that miss any hard requirement.\n- Among vendors that meet all hard requirements and fit the budget, select the lowest total cost.\n- If a vendor appears in more than one dated source and values conflict, use the newest dated source for that vendor.\n- Use local files only.\n\n--- output_contract.md ---\n# Deliverable Contract\n\nCreate an `answer/` folder in this task folder, then create these three files inside it. The format may be Markdown tables or concise labeled sections, but the paths, filenames, and required facts must be present.\n\n## `answer/source_resolution.md`\n\nRecord which source is current for each vendor where source dates matter.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- The recency rule from `requirements.md`.\n- The stale Northstar row in `vendor_quotes.csv` dated 2026-04-24.\n- The newer Northstar update in `northstar_update_2026-04-30.md`.\n- The effective Northstar terms used for screening: unit price, available quantity, delivery date, screen size, battery rating, rugged case status, and warranty months.\n\n## `answer/vendor_screen.md`\n\nScreen every vendor against the hard requirements.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- One row or entry for each vendor in `vendor_quotes.csv`.\n- For each vendor: effective source used, eligible `yes` or `no`, total cost if the vendor is otherwise eligible, and the blocking requirement when ineligible.\n- Budget status for any eligible vendor.\n\n## `answer/purchase_recommendation.md`\n\nWrite the final recommendation for the purchasing teammate.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- Selected vendor.\n- Quantity.\n- Unit price.\n- Total cost calculation.\n- Budget result.\n- Delivery date.\n- Short rejected-vendor summary.\n\nRules:\n\n- Use local files only.\n- Do not put the required deliverables in the task root; put them under `answer/`.\n- Extra scratch files are allowed, but scoring is based on the three named deliverables under `answer/`.\n\n--- vendor_quotes.csv ---\nvendor,quote_date,unit_price_usd,available_quantity,delivery_date,screen_inches,battery_hours,rugged_case_included,warranty_months,notes\nNorthstar,2026-04-24,185,12,2026-05-16,10.1,11,yes,12,\"Baseline quote. See any newer vendor-specific updates before deciding.\"\nAtlas,2026-04-27,168,12,2026-05-18,10.1,12,yes,12,\"Lowest baseline price but delivery date is after the need-by date.\"\nBrightPath,2026-04-26,171,12,2026-05-15,9.7,10,yes,12,\"Screen is below the minimum requirement.\"\nCobalt,2026-04-25,176,12,2026-05-16,10.1,9,yes,12,\"Battery rating is below the minimum requirement.\"\nDockside,2026-04-26,182,11,2026-05-14,10.1,13,yes,12,\"Only eleven units are available.\"\n\n--- northstar_update_2026-04-30.md ---\n# Northstar Update\n\nSource date: 2026-04-30\n\nVendor: Northstar\n\nNorthstar revised its quote after the baseline CSV was exported.\n\nUpdated terms:\n\n- Unit price: $178\n- Available quantity: 12\n- Delivery date: 2026-05-16\n- Screen size: 10.1 inches\n- Battery rating: 11 hours\n- Rugged case: included\n- Warranty: 12 months\n\nUse this source instead of the older `vendor_quotes.csv` Northstar row where they conflict."}, {"func_name": "run_in_task", "args": {"command": "cd /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/vendor_selection && mkdir -p answer", "timeout_seconds": 600}, "result": "(no output)"}, {"func_name": "run_in_task", "args": {"command": "cd /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/vendor_selection && cat > answer/source_resolution.md <<'EOF'\n# Source Resolution\n\nRecency rule from `requirements.md`: if a vendor appears in more than one dated source and values conflict, use the newest dated source for that vendor.\n\n## Vendor source determination\n\n| Vendor | Source(s) reviewed | Current source used | Reason |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Northstar | `vendor_quotes.csv` dated 2026-04-24; `northstar_update_2026-04-30.md` dated 2026-04-30 | `northstar_update_2026-04-30.md` | Northstar appears in more than one dated source, and the 2026-04-30 update is newer than the stale 2026-04-24 CSV row. |\n| Atlas | `vendor_quotes.csv` dated 2026-04-27 | `vendor_quotes.csv` | Only local source for Atlas. |\n| BrightPath | `vendor_quotes.csv` dated 2026-04-26 | `vendor_quotes.csv` | Only local source for BrightPath. |\n| Cobalt | `vendor_quotes.csv` dated 2026-04-25 | `vendor_quotes.csv` | Only local source for Cobalt. |\n| Dockside | `vendor_quotes.csv` dated 2026-04-26 | `vendor_quotes.csv` | Only local source for Dockside. |\n\n## Northstar stale vs. current source\n\n- Stale Northstar row: `vendor_quotes.csv` dated **2026-04-24**.\n- Newer Northstar update: `northstar_update_2026-04-30.md` dated **2026-04-30**.\n- Effective source used for screening Northstar: **`northstar_update_2026-04-30.md`**.\n\n## Effective Northstar terms used for screening\n\n| Field | Effective value |\n|---|---|\n| Unit price | $178 |\n| Available quantity | 12 |\n| Delivery date | 2026-05-16 |\n| Screen size | 10.1 inches |\n| Battery rating | 11 hours |\n| Rugged case status | Included |\n| Warranty | 12 months |\nEOF\n\ncat > answer/vendor_screen.md <<'EOF'\n# Vendor Screening\n\nOrder requirements from `requirements.md`: 12 rugged tablets, total budget no more than $2,200, delivery no later than 2026-05-17, screen size at least 10.0 inches, battery at least 10 hours, rugged case included, and warranty at least 12 months.\n\n| Vendor | Effective source used | Eligible | Total cost | Budget status | Blocking requirement when ineligible |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---|---|\n| Northstar | `northstar_update_2026-04-30.md` | yes | $2,136 | Within budget ($64 under $2,200) | None |\n| Atlas | `vendor_quotes.csv` | no | $2,016 | Would be within budget, but not eligible | Delivery date 2026-05-18 is later than need-by date 2026-05-17 |\n| BrightPath | `vendor_quotes.csv` | no | $2,052 | Would be within budget, but not eligible | Screen size 9.7 inches is below 10.0-inch minimum |\n| Cobalt | `vendor_quotes.csv` | no | $2,112 | Would be within budget, but not eligible | Battery rating 9 hours is below 10-hour minimum |\n| Dockside | `vendor_quotes.csv` | no | $2,184 for 12 units at quoted unit price | Not eligible | Available quantity is only 11, below required quantity of 12 |\n\n## Screening outcome\n\n- Fully eligible vendors within budget: **Northstar only**.\n- Lowest total cost among fully eligible vendors: **Northstar at $2,136**.\nEOF\n\ncat > answer/purchase_recommendation.md <<'EOF'\n# Purchase Recommendation\n\n## Recommended vendor\n\n- **Selected vendor:** Northstar\n- **Quantity:** 12 rugged tablets\n- **Unit price:** $178\n- **Total cost calculation:** 12 \u00d7 $178 = **$2,136**\n- **Budget result:** Within the $2,200 maximum; **$64 under budget**\n- **Delivery date:** 2026-05-16\n\n## Recommendation summary\n\nRecommend purchasing **12 rugged tablets from Northstar** using the updated terms in `northstar_update_2026-04-30.md`. Under the recency rule in `requirements.md`, the 2026-04-30 Northstar update supersedes the older 2026-04-24 CSV row. Northstar meets all hard requirements: quantity 12, screen size 10.1 inches, battery rating 11 hours, rugged case included, warranty 12 months, and delivery by the 2026-05-17 need-by date. The total cost is **$2,136**, which is the lowest total cost among fully eligible vendors.\n\n## Rejected vendor summary\n\n- **Atlas:** Rejected because delivery date 2026-05-18 misses the 2026-05-17 need-by date.\n- **BrightPath:** Rejected because screen size 9.7 inches is below the 10.0-inch minimum.\n- **Cobalt:** Rejected because battery rating 9 hours is below the 10-hour minimum.\n- **Dockside:** Rejected because only 11 units are available, below the required quantity of 12.\nEOF\n\nls -la answer && printf '\\n--- source_resolution.md ---\\n' && cat answer/source_resolution.md && printf '\\n--- vendor_screen.md ---\\n' && cat answer/vendor_screen.md && printf '\\n--- purchase_recommendation.md ---\\n' && cat answer/purchase_recommendation.md", "timeout_seconds": 600}, "result": "total 24\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 5 douglas  staff   160 Jun 15 19:46 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 8 douglas  staff   256 Jun 15 19:44 ..\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 douglas  staff  1231 Jun 15 19:46 purchase_recommendation.md\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 douglas  staff  1535 Jun 15 19:46 source_resolution.md\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 douglas  staff  1275 Jun 15 19:46 vendor_screen.md\n\n--- source_resolution.md ---\n# Source Resolution\n\nRecency rule from `requirements.md`: if a vendor appears in more than one dated source and values conflict, use the newest dated source for that vendor.\n\n## Vendor source determination\n\n| Vendor | Source(s) reviewed | Current source used | Reason |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Northstar | `vendor_quotes.csv` dated 2026-04-24; `northstar_update_2026-04-30.md` dated 2026-04-30 | `northstar_update_2026-04-30.md` | Northstar appears in more than one dated source, and the 2026-04-30 update is newer than the stale 2026-04-24 CSV row. |\n| Atlas | `vendor_quotes.csv` dated 2026-04-27 | `vendor_quotes.csv` | Only local source for Atlas. |\n| Brigh